    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so it's more of a slow build up. does the body have any natural way to fight it off or is it just something you have to manage with diet/meds? i just want to understand if my body is actually working against it or if it's just helpless to stop the buildup.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your body *does* have natural defenses, primarily through the HDL and healthy cellular processes that try to clear excess fats. However, when LDL levels are consistently high, these natural defenses can become overwhelmed by the sheer amount of cholesterol present. Therefore, lifestyle changes like diet and exercise are crucial for empowering your body's natural cleanup crew, but medication is often necessary to actively reduce the level of the substance causing the persistent buildup.",
      "source": "target",
